            "claim": "<Cite id=\"rt1-2022\" /> RT-1 predicts one robot action per timestep and commands the Everyday Robots mobile manipulator at 3 Hz. Each action dimension is mapped to one of 256 uniformly distributed bins within that variable’s bounds. Six input frames are observation history, not a six-action horizon. The paper announces open code; pretrained-weight availability is not disclosed in that statement.",
