                  "supportingPassage": "Instruction and image tokenization. The RT-1 architecture relies on a data-efficient and compact tokenization of images and language instruction.\nRT-1 tokenizes a history of 6 images by passing images through an ImageNet pretrained EfficientNet-B3 ( [Tan & Le, 2019](https://arxiv.org/html/2212.06817v2#bib.bib52 \"\")) model, which takes 6 images of resolution 300×300300\\\\times 300 as input and outputs a spatial feature map of shape 9×9×5129\\\\times 9\\\\times 512 from the final convolutional layer.\nUnlike [Reed et al. (2022)](https://arxiv.org/html/2212.06817v2#bib.bib42 \"\"), we do not patchify the images into visual tokens prior to feeding them to our Transformer backbone.\nWe instead flatten the output feature map from the EfficientNet into 8181 visual tokens which are passed on to the later layers of the network.\n\n"
                },
