                  "supportingPassage": "Original OpenVLA formulation. We use OpenVLA \\[ [23](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.19645#bib.bib23 \"\")\\] as our representative base VLA, a 7B-parameter manipulation policy created by fine-tuning the Prismatic VLM \\[ [21](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.19645#bib.bib21 \"\")\\] on 1M episodes from the Open X-Embodiment dataset \\[ [34](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.19645#bib.bib34 \"\")\\]. See Appendix [A-A](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.19645#A1.SS1 \"A-A Model Architecture Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Fine-Tuning Vision-Language-Action Models: Optimizing Speed and Success\") for architecture details. OpenVLA’s original training formulation uses autoregressive prediction of 7 discrete robot action tokens per timestep: 3 for position control, 3 for orientation control, and 1 for gripper control. It employs next-token prediction with cross-entropy loss as its learning objective, similar to language models. We explore alternative formulations including parallel decoding, continuous action representations, and learning objectives like L1 regression and diffusion modeling in the next few sections."
