                  "citationId": "octo-2024",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2405.12213v2",
                  "supportingPassage": "While Octo represents a step towards building generalist robot policies that work out-of-the-box on diverse robot setups, there remains work to improve the model, including better language conditioning, improved support for wrist cameras, and incorporating data beyond optimal demonstrations. We hope that Octo offers a simple launchpad for researchers and practitioners to access larger robotic datasets and leverage pretrained robotics models for efficient learning of new tasks and broad generalization."
