                  "citationId": "gemini-robotics-2025",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2503.20020v1",
                  "supportingPassage": "To this end, we introduce the Gemini Robotics family of embodied AI models, built on top of Gemini 2.0, our most advanced multimodal foundation model.\nWe first validate the performance and generality of the base Gemini 2.0’s innate embodied reasoning capabilities with a new open-source general embodied reasoning benchmark, ERQA.\nWe then introduce two models:\n\n[… noncontiguous retained passage …]\n\nWe present Gemini Robotics, an advanced Vision-Language-Action (VLA) generalist model capable of directly controlling robots.\n\n[… noncontiguous retained passage …]\n\nThis is made possible because Gemini Robotics builds on top of the Gemini Robotics-ER model, the second model we introduce in this work.\n\n[… noncontiguous retained passage …]\n\nGemini Robotics-ER (Embodied Reasoning) extends Gemini’s multimodal reasoning capabilities into the physical world, with enhanced spatial and temporal understanding. This enables capabilities relevant to robotics including object detection, pointing, trajectory and grasp prediction, as well as 3D understanding in the form of multi-view correspondence and 3D bounding box predictions."
