            "claim": "Kareer and colleagues report PI human/robot co-fine-tuning with 3D hand-position actions and no special transfer-learning mechanism, with transfer improving as robot pretraining quantity/diversity grows. Zheng and colleagues’ EgoScale combines relative wrist/retargeted hand supervision and aligned human–robot mid-training, with scale and alignment complementary in their evaluated setting. Neither proves a universal scale-alone versus hard-alignment dichotomy.",
