                  "supportingPassage": "- **New VLM backbone:** Cosmos-Reason2-2B (Qwen3-VL architecture), replacing the Eagle backbone used in N1.6. Supports flexible resolution and encodes images in their native aspect ratio without padding.\n[Separate literal excerpt from the same retained response]\n| [`nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B`](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B) | Base | See [pretrain tags](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/getting_started/policy.md#--embodiment-tag) | Base model (3B params) — zero-shot inference on pretrain embodiments, or finetune for new tasks |\n[Separate literal excerpt from the same retained response]\n- State and action dimensions expanded from `29` to `132`, and `action_horizon` expanded from `16` to `40`.\n- Action head remains flow-matching DiT, but changes from `32` to `16` diffusion layers and adds newer N1.7 behavior options.\n- Dataset input handling now supports multiple dataset paths and `ds_weights_alpha` for dataset mixtures.\n- The rollout CLI flag was renamed from `--action-horizon` to `--execution-horizon` to clarify how many predicted actions are executed per policy call.\n- Server/client transport\n[Separate literal excerpt from the same retained response]\n1. **Relative EEF Action Space** — N1.7 adopts a relative end-effector action space shared across robot and human embodiments. Representing actions as deltas from the current pose (rather than absolute targets) improves generalization and is a key factor in the model's cross-embodiment performance. See [`getting_started/finetune_new_embodiment.md`](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/getting_started/finetune_new_embodiment.md) for guidance on configuring relative EEF for your own robot."
                },
                {
