                  "supportingPassage": "Another important aspect to consider is how our method handles demonstrations compared to others.\nTo compare against the mentioned baselines, we collected 200 demonstrations for each task. Note this number is substantially larger than the number of offline demonstrations in our method, which is usually around 20-30 in the offline replay buffer.\nFor Residual RL and IBRL, we trained behavior cloning (BC) policies with these demonstrations to feed into their algorithm pipeline. For DAPG, we stored these 200 demonstrations in a separate buffer and regularized the policy actions towards them.\nOverall, our method consistently outperformed these baselines by large margins, as shown in Table. [1](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2410.21845#S4.T1 \"Table 1 ‣ 4.3 Experimental Results ‣ 4 Experiment Results ‣ Precise and Dexterous Robotic Manipulation via Human-in-the-Loop Reinforcement Learning\")."
