            "claim": "On expert data, their similar-performance statement is a worst-case result without additional environment-structure assumptions. They also identify conditions under which offline RL can improve on that result; Section 6 leaves understanding when BC is preferable as further work . **Editorial recommendation:** for a teleoperation dataset, start with a supervised [behavior-cloning baseline](/manipulation/bc-foundations) as the simpler starting point, then test a tuned offline RL alternative under the same evaluation protocol. That is this article's advice, not Kumar and colleagues' endorsement of BC or a guarantee that short-horizon expert data favors cloning.",
