            "claim": "Gupta and colleagues’ MTRF sequences learned task-specific policies with a designer-provided task graph; recovery tasks enable retries of valve reorientation and pipe insertion on a D’Hand/Sawyer system. The paper reports training without manual episode resets in these setups, not an absence of human setup or a general safety guarantee. Supplied rewards/task graphs, initial object placement, in-hand motion capture, scripted pickup-arm motion and pipe-insertion control restrictions remain explicit. Successful upstream tasks must produce valid downstream starting states; full downstream state coverage is not guaranteed.",
