                  "supportingPassage": "[Retained literal excerpt minitaur-training; lines 363–365]\nOur method successfully learns to walk from 160k control steps, or approximately 400 rollouts. Each rollout has the maximum length of 500 steps (equivalent to 10 seconds) and can terminate early if the robot falls. The whole training process takes about two hours. [Figure 7](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/1812.11103#S7.F7 \"Fig. 7 ‣ VII-B Results ‣ VII Learning in the Real World ‣ Learning to Walk via Deep Reinforcement Learning\") shows the learning curve,\nThe performance is slightly less than the simulation, potentially due to fewer collected samples.\nPlease refer to the supplemental v\n\n[Retained literal excerpt minitaur-resets; lines 55–55]\nOnce training is started, minimal human intervention is needed, except for the need to reset the robot if it falls or runs out of free space."
