                  "partId": "w7-zero-shot-60pct",
                  "citationId": "play2perfect-2026",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2606.26428",
                  "supportingPassage": "We demonstrate zero-shot sim-to-real transfer, achieving 60% success on tight insertions with only 0.5 mm contact clearance, and over 50% success on long-horizon multi-part assembly and screwing. [...] The real-world results show the same trend. At 10 mm clearance, Play2Perfect achieves 100% success compared to 60% for Play-only . At 2 mm clearance, Play2Perfect achieves 90% success while Play-only drops to 20%. At 0.5 mm clearance, Play2Perfect still succeeds 60% of the time, whereas Play-only fails completely. Table 1: Real-World Assembly Results. Play2Perfect transfers zero-shot to real-world insertion, multi-part assembly, and screwing tasks. ... Tight-Insertion ... 10mm 2mm 0.5mm ... Success Rate 10/10 9/10 6/10 ... Setup. We evaluate whether assembly policies finetuned in simulation can transfer zero-shot to the real world. We deploy Play2Perfect on Tight-Insertion , Assemble-Beam , and Screw-Leg , using FoundationPose [ 59 ] for object pose tracking and no real-world finetuning."
                },
