            "note": "Correction reviewed 2026-09-09T12:44:02.510Z by agent:0d32fee8/integrator against retained original responses, not a new retrieval. The preserved HTML date is August 2025; the introduction, simulation and next-steps sections describe research policies, whole-body manipulation including locomotion, and hardware deployment, not all-stack replacement. The Policy section explicitly states 450M parameters, diffusion transformer, flow matching, and proprioception/images/language conditioning. These are the reported model inputs and training objective. The four-stage process collects hardware and simulation teleoperation, then processes, annotates and curates it. The later quality-assurance discussion confirms filtering demonstrations. The caption gives 30 Hz actions. The Policy section separately gives 30 Hz images, 48 predicted actions/1.6 seconds, and generally 24 executed/0.8 seconds at 1x per inference. Execution-speed adaptation precludes treating 30 Hz as an inference frequency. The teleoperation section names MPC and explicitly says neural policies use that same robot control interface. This establishes interface reuse, not an undisclosed fallback protocol or every downstream controller. Bibliography: Spot personal byline and RAI corporate-name expansion remain unestablished; the four explicit LBM Blog Authors are preserved despite JSON-LD mrodin. No whole-P1 or article credit. Original four cells are retained in boston-control-original-history-20260909. Source proof: validation/brand-v2-editorial/source-recovery-20260906/convergence-boston-dynamics-control-integration-20260909/source-proof.json.",
