                  "citationId": "kungfubot-2025",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2506.12851",
                  "supportingPassage": "### C.5 Curriculum Learning\n\nTo imitate high-dynamic motions, we introduce two curriculum mechanisms: a termination curriculum that gradually reduces tracking error tolerance, and a penalty curriculum that progressively increases the weight of regularization terms, promoting more stable and physically plausible behaviors.\n\n- •\n\n\nTermination Curriculum:\nThe episode is terminated early when the humanoid’s motion deviates from the reference beyond a termination threshold θ\\\\theta. During training, this threshold is gradually decreased to increase the difficulty:\n\n\n\n\n\n|     |     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | θ←clip⁡(θ⋅(1−δ),θmin,θmax),\\\\theta\\\\leftarrow\\\\mathrm{clip}\\\\left(\\\\theta\\\\cdot(1-\\\\delta),\\ \\\\theta\\_{\\\\min},\\ \\\\theta\\_{\\\\max}\\\\right), |  | (19) |\n\n\n\nwhere the initial threshold θ=1.5\\\\theta=1.5, with bounds θmin=0.3\\\\theta\\_{\\\\min}=0.3, θmax=2.0\\\\theta\\_{\\\\max}=2.0, and decay rate δ=2.5×10−5\\\\delta=2.5\\\\times 10^{-5}.\n\n- •\n\n\nPenalty Curriculum:\nTo facilitate learning in the early training stages while gradually enforcing stronger regularization, we introduce a scaling factor α\\\\alpha that increases progressively to modulate the influence of the penalty term:\n\n\n\n\n\n|     |     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | α←clip⁡(α⋅(1+δ),αmin,αmax),r^penalty←α⋅rpenalty,\\\\alpha\\\\leftarrow\\\\mathrm{clip}\\\\left(\\\\alpha\\\\cdot(1+\\\\delta),\\ \\\\alpha\\_{\\\\min},\\ \\\\alpha\\_{\\\\max}\\\\right),\\\\hskip 8.50012pt\\\\hat{r}\\_{\\\\rm{penalty}}\\\\leftarrow\\\\alpha\\\\cdot r\\_{\\\\rm{penalty}}, |  | (20) |\n\n\n\n\n\nwhere the initial penalty scale α=0.1\\\\alpha=0.1, with bounds αmin=0.0\\\\alpha\\_{\\\\min}=0.0, αmax=1.0\\\\alpha\\_{\\\\max}=1.0, and growth rate δ=1.0×10−4\\\\delta=1.0\\\\times 10^{-4}.\n\n"
                },
