                  "supportingPassage": "| Batch size | 98304 (4096x24) |\n| --- | --- |\n| Mini-bach size | 24576 (4096x6) |\n| --- | --- |\n| Number of epochs | 5 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Clip range | 0.2 |\n| Entropy coefficient | 0.01 |\n| Discount factor | 0.99 |\n| GAE discount factor | 0.95 |\n| Desired KL-divergence k​l∗kl^{\\*} | 0.01 |\n| Learning rate α\\\\alpha | adaptive∗ |\n\nTable 3: PPO hyper-parameters used for the training of the tested policy. (\\*) Similarly to \\[ [9](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2109.11978#bib.bib9 \"\")\\], we use an adaptive learning rate based on the KL-divergence, the corresponding algorithm is described in Alg. [1](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2109.11978#alg1 \"Algorithm 1 ‣ A.4 PPO Hyper-Parameters ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning to Walk in Minutes Using Massively Parallel Deep Reinforcement Learning\")Algorithm 1 Adaptive learning rate computation.\n\nk​l←K​L​(πn​e​w,πo​l​d)kl\\\\leftarrow KL(\\\\pi\\_{new},\\\\pi\\_{old})\n\nifk​l>2​k​l∗kl>2kl^{\\*}then\n\nα←max⁡(10−5,α/1.5)\\\\alpha\\\\leftarrow\\\\max(10^{-5},\\\\alpha/1.5)\n\nelse\n\nifk​l<0.5​k​l∗kl<0.5kl^{\\*}then\n\nα←min⁡(10−2,1.5​α)\\\\alpha\\\\leftarrow\\\\min(10^{-2},1.5\\\\alpha)\n\nendif\n\nendif\n\n### A.5 Noise Level in Observations\n"
