            "note": "Current correction review 2026-09-12T22:31:35.549Z by agent:d9816a12/integrator; no new retrieval. ArXiv metadata and body name nine ordered authors and the March 2026 v3 revision after March 2025 initial submission. The venue comment says to appear, not presented. Abs/body abstracts differ; the body anonymous-review placeholder is not evidence of a version or venue change. III-A/B specifies forward finite differences for dynamics/residual Jacobians, analytical norm derivatives and approximate cost Hessians. One warm-started update returns without convergence checks; plain iLQR is not an exact-derivative or fully converged optimizer claim. IV-B and V-A include low-level PD in model and hardware and OptiTrack/joint fusion via ROS/SDK. Floating-base velocities use filtered pose differences. Laboratory motion capture is not onboard-only deployment. V-A specifies a 20-core 13th-generation i9, approximately 50-Hz iLQR and 300-Hz feedback, default 0.35-s/100-Hz model, and separate approximately 3-ms Python overhead. Repeated math text in the tool rendering is normalized in prose, while the literal duplicated rendering is retained in evidence. V-B/C supports Go1/Go2 gait tracking and bipedal quadruped behavior, with gait costs rather than hard contact constraints. The independently rechecked retained Fig.1 caption explicitly identifies the Go1 hind-leg/handstand demonstrations and is added to this same required pair. V-D identifies H1 periodic trotting, 0.5-s horizon, disabled upper-body DoFs with unreliable relative encoders, ten active joints and four foot contact points with other body collision checking disabled. Whole-body is bounded by these implementation choices. IV-A raises impratio from 1 to 100; approximately 10-to-20-ms iterations refer to a separate 12th-generation i7 test. IV-C records gantry recovery without TV-LQR in the eight-second comparison, not autonomous recovery or general reliability. IV-D optional derivative skipping and center