                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04613",
                  "supportingPassage": "# Title:Whole-Body Model-Predictive Control of Legged Robots with MuJoCo\n\nAuthors: [John Z. Zhang](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Zhang,+J+Z), [Taylor A. Howell](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Howell,+T+A), [Zeji Yi](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Yi,+Z), [Chaoyi Pan](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Pan,+C), [Guanya Shi](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Shi,+G), [Guannan Qu](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Qu,+G), [Tom Erez](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Erez,+T), [Yuval Tassa](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Tassa,+Y), [Zachary Manchester](https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&query=Manchester,+Z)\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Whole-Body Model-Predictive Control of Legged Robots with MuJoCo, by John Z. Zhang and 8 other authors\n\n[View PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.04613) [HTML (experimental)](https://arxiv.org/html/2503.04613v3)\n\n> Abstract:We demonstrate the surprising real-world effectiveness of a very simple approach to whole-body model-predictive control (MPC) of quadruped and humanoid robots: the iterative LQR (iLQR) algorithm with MuJoCo dynamics and finite-difference approximated derivatives. Building upon the previous success of model-based behavior synthesis and control of locomotion and manipulation tasks with MuJoCo in simulation, we show that these policies can easily generalize to the real world with few sim-to-real considerations. Our baseline method achieves real-time whole-body MPC on a variety of hardware experiments, including dynamic quadruped locomotion, quadruped walking on two legs, and full-sized humanoid bipedal locomotion. We hope this easy-to-reproduce hardware baseline lowers the barrier to entry for real-world whole-body MPC research and contributes to accelerating research velocity in the community. Our code and experiment videos will be available online at: [this https URL](https://johnzhang3.github.io/mujoco_ilqr)\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Comments: | to appear at ICRA 2026 |\n| Subjects: | Robotics (cs.RO); Systems and Control (eess.SY) |\n| Cite as: | [arXiv:2503.04613](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04613) \\[cs.RO\\] |\n|  | (or [arXiv:2503.04613v3](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04613v3) \\[cs.RO\\] for this version) |\n|  | [https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.04613](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.04613)<br>Focus to learn more<br>arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite |\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: John Zhang \\[ [view email](https://arxiv.org/show-email/e5c2777c/2503.04613)\\]\n\n**[\\[v1\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04613v1)**\nThu, 6 Mar 2025 16:59:06 UTC (22,361 KB)\n\n**[\\[v2\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04613v2)**\nSat, 18 Oct 2025 15:26:32 UTC (4,140 KB)\n\n**\\[v3\\]**\nFri, 6 Mar 2026 17:45:16 UTC (4,133 KB)"
