            "note": "Correction reviewed 2026-09-09T12:44:02.510Z by agent:0d32fee8/integrator against retained original responses, not a new retrieval. The dated Spot document retains model-based locomotion while removing parallel MPC evaluation through its learned policy. Its separate research limitations prevent a timeless universal hybrid claim. The separate dated Atlas document describes language-conditioned whole-body manipulation and reuses the MPC-based teleoperation interface. Both source documents are necessary for this two-robot statement. Bibliography: Spot personal byline and RAI corporate-name expansion remain unestablished; the four explicit LBM Blog Authors are preserved despite JSON-LD mrodin. No whole-P1 or article credit. Original four cells are retained in boston-control-original-history-20260909. Source proof: validation/brand-v2-editorial/source-recovery-20260906/convergence-boston-dynamics-control-integration-20260909/source-proof.json.",
