                  "supportingPassage": "{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"mrodin\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/a4d76fffcd30181801eb34e2584caf90\"},\"headline\":\"Starting on the Right Foot with Reinforcement Learning\",\"datePublished\":\"2024-03-19T14:02:45+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2024-06-27T18:49:50+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/\"},\"wordCount\":1739,\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/03\\/spot-unstable-ground-scaled.jpg\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/\",\"name\":\"Starting on the Right Foot with Reinforcement Learning | Boston Dynamics\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#primaryimage\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/03\\/spot-unstable-ground-scaled.jpg\",\"datePublished\":\"2024-03-19T14:02:45+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2024-06-27T18:49:50+00:00\",\"description\":\"We’ve integrated reinforcement learning into Spot’s locomotion to enable the robot to handle more and more real-world variability.\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#breadcrumb\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"ReadAction\",\"target\":[\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#primaryimage\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/03\\/spot-unstable-ground-scaled.jpg\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2024\\/03\\/spot-unstable-ground-scaled.jpg\",\"width\":2560,\"height\":1807,\"caption\":\"Spot walks across on unstable terrain\"},{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/starting-on-the-right-foot-with-reinforcement-learning\\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Starting on the Right Foot with Reinforcement Learning\"}]},{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#website\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/\",\"name\":\"Boston Dynamics\",\"description\":\"Changing your idea of what robots can do.\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/?s={search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":{\"@type\":\"PropertyValueSpecification\",\"valueRequired\":true,\"valueName\":\"search_term_string\"}}],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/a4d76fffcd30181801eb34e2584caf90\",\"name\":\"mrodin\",\"image\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"caption\":\"mrodin\"}}]}\n\nArchitecting things this way has multiple benefits. First, it allows us to take advantage of our existing model-based locomotion controller to solve the part of the problem it handles well, while focusing learning on the part of the strategy that is harder to program. Second, it reduces the computational complexity of the production controller by removing the need to run multiple MPC instances in parallel.\n\nWhile a hybrid control strategy that leverages both a model predictive controller and a learned policy is proving effective at expanding and robustifying robotic capabilities, it largely imposes the limitations of the modeling on the full control system. To unlock totally new capabilities or be tolerant in scenarios that excessively violate the assumptions of the models, we are actively exploring and testing totally different architectures."
