                  "sourceUrl": "https://bostondynamics.com/blog/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing/",
                  "supportingPassage": "{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"mrodin\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/a4d76fffcd30181801eb34e2584caf90\"},\"headline\":\"Large Behavior Models and Atlas Find New Footing\",\"datePublished\":\"2025-08-20T15:53:19+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-08-20T18:47:30+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/\"},\"wordCount\":2293,\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/08\\/atlas-tri-blog.jpg\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/\",\"name\":\"Large Behavior Models and Atlas Find New Footing | Boston Dynamics\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#primaryimage\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/08\\/atlas-tri-blog.jpg\",\"datePublished\":\"2025-08-20T15:53:19+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-08-20T18:47:30+00:00\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#breadcrumb\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"ReadAction\",\"target\":[\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#primaryimage\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/08\\/atlas-tri-blog.jpg\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/08\\/atlas-tri-blog.jpg\",\"width\":1530,\"height\":1080,\"caption\":\"The Atlas folds a leg from a Spot robot\"},{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/blog\\/large-behavior-models-atlas-find-new-footing\\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Large Behavior Models and Atlas Find New Footing\"}]},{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#website\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/\",\"name\":\"Boston Dynamics\",\"description\":\"Changing your idea of what robots can do.\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/?s={search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":{\"@type\":\"PropertyValueSpecification\",\"valueRequired\":true,\"valueName\":\"search_term_string\"}}],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/bostondynamics.com\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/a4d76fffcd30181801eb34e2584caf90\",\"name\":\"mrodin\",\"image\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/secure.gravatar.com\\/avatar\\/a4cacff82401ce3a50e4b86e9dd37c58c3f484002a6ff490dd53020254faba30?s=96&d=mm&r=g\",\"caption\":\"mrodin\"}}]}\n\nWe are excited to share some of our progress on developing [Large Behavior Models (LBMs)](https://toyotaresearchinstitute.github.io/lbm1/) for [Atlas](https://bostondynamics.com/atlas/) ®. This work is part of a [collaboration](https://pressroom.toyota.com/boston-dynamics-and-toyota-research-institute-announce-partnership-to-advance-robotics-research/) between AI research teams at Toyota Research Institute (TRI) and Boston Dynamics. We have been building end-to-end language-conditioned policies that enable Atlas to accomplish long-horizon manipulation tasks.\n\nThese policies are able to take full advantage of the capabilities of the humanoid form factor, including taking steps, precisely positioning its feet, crouching, shifting its center of mass, and avoiding self-collisions, all of which we have found to be critical to solving realistic mobile manipulation tasks.\n\nControlling the robot in a fluid, dynamic, and dexterous manner is crucial, and we have invested heavily in our teleoperation system to address these needs. The system is built on Boston Dynamics’s MPC system, which has previously been deployed for use-cases ranging from [parkour](https://bostondynamics.com/blog/flipping-the-script-with-atlas/), [dance](https://youtu.be/fn3KWM1kuAw?feature=shared), and both [practical](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/SFKM-Rxiqzg) and [impractical manipulation](https://bostondynamics.com/blog/picking-up-momentum/). This control system allows us to perform precise manipulation while maintaining balance and avoiding self-collisions, enabling us to push the boundaries of what we can do with the Atlas hardware.\n\nOur neural network policies use the same control interface to the robot as the teleoperation system, which made it easy to reuse model architectures we had developed previously (for policies that didn’t involve locomotion), simply by augmenting the action representation."
