            "note": "Abstract prints verbatim: 'adapting a large pretrained video model (Cosmos-Predict2) into an effective robot policy through a single stage of post-training on the robot demonstration data collected on the target platform, with no architectural modifications'; actions and future state images are generated 'encoded as latent frames'. 'The same idea on top of the Cosmos backbone' is the article's editorial comparison to WorldVLA, not a paper-printed clause; abstract-page tier only, nothing beyond the abstract is certified.",
