            "note": "Abstract prints verbatim: 'we explore a new framework of learning a world model, OccWorld, in the 3D Occupancy space to simultaneously predict the movement of the ego car and the evolution of the surrounding scenes' and 'OccWorld also produces competitive planning results without using instance and map supervision.' Precision: 'occupancy grid' is the article's term; the paper prints '3D Occupancy space'/'3D occupancy'.",
            "compound": {
              "planId": "taxonomy-18-occworld-20260916h",
              "evidence": [
                {
                  "partId": "t18-occworld-occupancy-evolution",
                  "citationId": "occworld-2023",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.16038",
                  "supportingPassage": "In this paper, we explore a new framework of learning a world model, OccWorld, in the 3D Occupancy space to simultaneously predict the movement of the ego car and the evolution of the surrounding scenes. We propose to learn a world model based on 3D occupancy rather than 3D bounding boxes and segmentation maps for three reasons: 1) expressiveness. 3D occupancy can describe the more fine-grained 3D structure of the scene; 2) efficiency. 3D occupancy is more economical to obtain (e.g., from sparse LiDAR points). 3) versatility. 3D occupancy can adapt to both vision and LiDAR. [...] OccWorld also produces competitive planning results without using instance and map supervision."
                },
                {
                  "partId": "t18-occworld-planning-no-supervision",
                  "citationId": "occworld-2023",
