                  "supportingPassage": "##### Attentive Probe.\n\nWe train an 4-layers attentive probe on top of the frozen encoder output using the training data from each task. Our attentive probe is composed of four transformer blocks, the last of which replaces standard self-attention with a cross-attention layer using a learnable query token. Following standard practice, several clips with a fixed number of frames are sampled from a video during inference. The classification logits are then averaged across clips. We keep the resolution similar to the one used for V-JEPA 2 pretraining. We ablate the number of layers of our attentive probe in [SectionC.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#A3.SS2 \"C.2 Additional Results ‣ Appendix C Visual Classification ‣ V-JEPA 2: Self-Supervised Video Models Enable Understanding, Prediction and Planning\"), and also provide full details on the number of clips, clip size, and other hyperparameters used in the downstream tasks.\n\nTable 4: Action and Object Classification. We report the classification performance of V-JEPA 2 models pretrained on 64 frames at resolution 256×256256\\\\times 256 for all models, except V-JEPA 2 ViT-g384 which was pretrained at resolution 384×384384\\\\times 384, on action and object classification, and compare their performance with state-of-art image and video encoders. All models follow the same evaluation protocol except for V-JEPA 2 ViT-g384. We use 256×256256\\\\times 256 resolution with 16×2×316\\\\times 2\\\\times 3 inputs for SSv2 (16 frames clip, 2 temporal crops, 3 spatial crops), 16×8×316\\\\times 8\\\\times 3 for K400, 32×8×332\\\\times 8\\\\times 3 for COIN and 32×4×332\\\\times 4\\\\times 3 for Diving-48 and Jester. V-JEPA 2 ViT-g384 uses a higher resolution of 384×384384\\\\times 384 for all six tasks, and additionally uses 64×2×364\\\\times 2\\\\times 3 inputs for SSv2 and 32x8x3 inputs for COIN. Our V-JEPA 2 ViT-g significantly outperforms other vision encoders on motion understanding tasks and is competitive on appearance tasks. It achieves the best average performance of 87.587.5 across all image and videos encoders. V-JEPA 2 ViT-g384 further improves results consistently across tasks, reaching 88.288.2 average performance.\n∗\\*: PEcoreG achieves an accuracy 89.8%89.8\\\\% on ImageNet using an attentive probe and input resoluton of 448448px ( [Bolya et al., 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib10 \"\")). We use an input resolution of 256256px and a different probe architecture in our case.\n\n|     |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  | Motion Understanding | Appearance Understanding |\n| Method | Param. | Avg. | SSv2 | Diving-48 | Jester | K400 | COIN | IN1K |\n| Results Reported in the Literature |  |  |  |\n| VideoMAEv2( [Wang et al., 2023](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib111 \"\")) | 1B | – | 56.1 | – | – | 82.8 | – | 71.4 |\n| InternVideo2-1B( [Wang et al., 2024b](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib113 \"\")) | 1B | – | 67.3 | – | – | 87.9 | – | – |\n| InternVideo2-6B( [Wang et al., 2024b](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib113 \"\")) | 6B | – | 67.7 | – | – | 88.8 | – | – |\n| VideoPrism( [Zhao et al., 2024](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib128 \"\")) | 1B | – | 68.5 | 71.3 | – | 87.6 | – | – |\n| Image Encoders Evaluated Using the Same Protocol |  |  |  |\n| DINOv2( [Darcet et al., 2024](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib25 \"\")) | 1.1B | 81.1 | 50.7 | 82.5 | 93.4 | 83.6 | 90.7 | 86.1 |\n| PEcoreG( [Bolya et al., 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib10 \"\")) | 1.9B | 82.3 | 55.4 | 76.9 | 90.0 | 88.5 | 95.3 | 87.6∗ |\n| SigLIP2( [Tschannen et al., 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib107 \"\")) | 1.2B | 81.1 | 49.9 | 75.3 | 91.0 | 87.3 | 95.1 | 88.0 |\n| Video Encoders Evaluated Using the Same Protocol |  |  |  |\n| V-JEPA ViT-H( [Bardes et al., 2024](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib6 \"\")) | 600M | 85.2 | 74.3 | 87.9 | 97.7 | 84.5 | 87.1 | 80.0 |\n| InternVideo2s2-1B( [Wang et al., 2024b](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09985#bib.bib113 \"\")) | 1B | 87.0 | 69.7 | 86.4 | 97.0 | 89.4 | 93.8 | 85.8 |\n| V-JEPA 2 ViT-L | 300M | 86.0 | 73.7 | 89.0 | 97.6 | 85.1 | 86.8 | 83.5 |\n| V-JEPA 2 ViT-H | 600M | 86.4 | 74.0 | 89.8 | 97.7 | 85.3 | 87.9 | 83.8 |\n| V-JEPA 2 ViT-g | 1B | 87.5 | 75.3 | 90.1 | 97.7 | 86.6 | 90.7 | 84.6 |\n| V-JEPA 2 ViT-g384 | 1B | 88.2 | 77.3 | 90.2 | 97.8 | 87.3 | 91.1 | 85.1 |\n\n"
