            "claim": "Snyder et al.'s observed v4 reports up to 32% fewer evaluation trials versus state-of-the-art sequential baselines with stated statistical assurances under its i.i.d. binary-outcome, risk-budget and horizon assumptions. TRI used sequential binary-policy testing but explicitly adopted Lai's test, not Snyder's STEP; its task-progress analysis uses Welch's t-test.",
