                  "supportingPassage": "| WidowX+BridgeEvaluation Setup | Policy | Put Spoon on Towel | Put Carrot on Plate | Stack Green Block on Yellow Block | Put Eggplant in Yellow Basket |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Grasp Spoon | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Success | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Grasp Carrot | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Success | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Grasp Green Block | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Success | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Grasp Eggplant | | |     |\n| --- |\n| Success | |\n| Real Eval | RT-1-X | 0.042 | 0.000 | 0.167 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.033 | 0.000 |\n| Octo-Base | 0.500 | 0.333 | 0.500 | 0.250 | 0.292 | 0.000 | 0.400 | 0.233 |\n| Octo-Small | 0.542 | 0.417 | 0.208 | 0.083 | 0.583 | 0.125 | 0.700 | 0.433 |\n| SIMPLER Eval(Visual Matching) | RT-1-X | 0.167 | 0.000 | 0.208 | 0.042 | 0.083 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| Octo-Base | 0.347 | 0.125 | 0.528 | 0.083 | 0.319 | 0.000 | 0.667 | 0.431 |\n| Octo-Small | 0.778 | 0.472 | 0.278 | 0.097 | 0.403 | 0.042 | 0.875 | 0.569 |\n| MMRV↓\\\\downarrow | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| Pearson rr↑\\\\uparrow | 0.778 | 0.827 | 0.995 | 0.575 | 0.964 | 1.000 | 0.995 | 0.990 |\n\nTABLE V: Real-world and SAPIEN simulation evaluation results for the WidowX + Bridge setup. We report both the final success rate (“Success”) along with partial success (e.g., “Grasp Spoon”).\n\nIn [TableIV](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#A4.T4 \"In Appendix D Full Results for Real-and-Sim Relative Policy Performance Correlation Experiments ‣ Evaluating Real-World Robot Manipulation Policies in Simulation\") and [TableV](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#A4.T5 \"In Appendix D Full Results for Real-and-Sim Relative Policy Performance Correlation Experiments ‣ Evaluating Real-World Robot Manipulation Policies in Simulation\"), we present full evaluation results for our experiments in Sec. [VI-B](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#S6.SS2 \"VI-B SIMPLER Environments Show Strong Performance Correlations with Real-World Evaluations ‣ VI Experimental Results ‣ Evaluating Real-World Robot Manipulation Policies in Simulation\"), which demonstrate that SIMPLER environments show strong performance relationship correlations with real-world evaluations."
