                  "partId": "simpler-limitations",
                  "citationId": "simpler-2024",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941",
                  "supportingPassage": "Limitations. Our current set of environments has several limitations. First, we focus our evaluations on rigid-object manipulation tasks, as their physics are most straight-forward to simulate with modern physics simulators. Much recent work in robotic manipulation has demonstrated impressive tasks that go beyond rigid object manipulation \\[ [20](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#bib.bib20 \"\"), [10](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#bib.bib10 \"\"), [33](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#bib.bib33 \"\")\\]. Extending simulated evaluation beyond rigid object tasks, e.g., by leveraging recent work on soft-object physics simulation \\[ [38](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.05941#bib.bib38 \"\")\\], is an exciting avenue for future work.\nAdditionally, our current “green-screening” approach is limited to fixed cameras and does not accurately capture object shadows and other visual details. Finally, our current pipeline for generating simulated evaluation environments involves some manual effort in curating assets and assembling scenes. Enabling a fully-automatic and more scalable pipeline for creating thousands of realistic simulated environments is an ambitious goal for future work."
                }
