ons were up 2% to 128,899 units. The share of the total\ninstallations was up 1 percentage point to 24%. Demand for electronics for all kinds of\nengineering, including automotive and industrial machinery and for consumer\nelectronics, has been growing strongly for many years. Global production capacity has\nbeen ramped up and so has the industry’s robot demand. From 2019 to 2024, the\ncompound annual growth rate (CAGR) was +8%.\n\nThe automotive industry was the second largest customer of industrial robots in 2024,\njust some 2,800 units shy of the electronics industry. Demand was down 7% to 126,088\nunits. The automotive industry invested in the transition from combustion engines to\nalternative drives, but decreasing demand for battery electric vehicles currently limits the\nneed for capacity expansion. From 2019 to 2024, annual installations in the automotive\nindustry increased by 5% on average each year (CAGR). After several years of\ncontinuous decline, down to 21% in 2020, the share of the automotive industry in the\ntotal installations was 25% in 2022 and 2023 and 24% in 2024."
