            "claim": "Ratliff et al. and Schulman et al. describe local trajectory optimization requiring an initial trajectory, including infeasible seeds, with failures and initialization dependence. Ratliff et al. describe PRM/RRT as typically used in a two-phase feasible-path/refinement process; Schulman et al. distinguish refinement from planning from scratch. This is attribution to those papers, not a claim of a standard contemporary industrial pipeline or a deterministic/collision-free guarantee.",
            "line": 207,
            "verdict": "C",
            "outcome": "passing",
            "citationId": "",
            "sourceUrl": "",
            "supportingPassage": "",
            "evidenceFailures": [],
            "sourceChecked": "consistent with ratliff-2009 / schulman-2013 framings",
            "note": "Retained CHOMP PDF GET2026-09-13T09:42:20.675954–09:42:25.181487Z and TrajOpt PDF GET09:42:25.261839–09:42:27.243177Z: original HTTP200/no redirects, zero new retrieval. Both full documents report local optimization from initial trajectories, including infeasible seeds, and failed queries. Neither establishes guaranteed feasibility or global optimality. Ratliff's introduction supplies the PRM/RRT two-phase account; Schulman's introduction separately distinguishes refinement and planning from scratch. The conjunction supports attribution to these papers, not a present-day industrial census. CHOMP's straight-line/RRT comparison is conditioned on collision-removal success; TrajOpt's single/multiple starts change success rates. Both sources are required and neither warrants a collision-free-seed or mandatory-preplanner rule. Current review 2026-09-13T14:32:03.076Z. CHOMP eight-page preprint is not certified identical to the six-page landing publication; Matthew/Matt byline forms remain distinct. TrajOpt retained unversioned ten-page body does not independently certify edition history. Full extracted text and CHOMP images1/2/5, TrajOpt1/3/6/8 inspected; eleven page images remain uninspected. Article lastReviewed unchanged; whole P1, readers and independent acceptance remain open.",
            "compound": {
              "planId": "trajectory-optimization-14-20260913",
              "evidence": [
                {
                  "partId": "mp14-local-initialization",
                  "citationId": "ratliff-2009",
