            "sourceChecked": "kaess-2012 (title: \"iSAM2: Incremental smoothing and mapping using the Bayes tree\")",
            "note": "Original four-cell tuple (JSON): {\"claim\":\"iSAM2 organizes the graph into the Bayes tree so updates stay local\",\"sourceChecked\":\"kaess-2012 (title: \\\"iSAM2: Incremental smoothing and mapping using the Bayes tree\\\")\",\"verdict\":\"V\",\"note\":\"\"}. Original tuple SHA256: 1a8e9943afb0798c16cd9e3cfb3ab133edab41e8d681860a5ac69baa292e990b. Integrator review 2026-09-13T16:10:05.818Z: The retained iSAM2 draft describes Bayes-tree incremental nonlinear least squares with Gaussian noise models, incremental reordering and relinearization. The author page bridges this April 6, 2011 draft to February 2012 publication, not version-of-record bytes. The update description and inspected page 9 identify affected cliques and ancestors to the root, with unaffected subtrees reattached. Omitting ancestors would repeat the false universally local-work interpretation. The retained update discussion explicitly permits top-of-tree estimate changes to propagate downward. Reusing a subtree factorization is not a promise that its state estimates remain fixed. The source distinguishes relinearization and partial-state-update thresholds and their computation/accuracy tradeoffs. Near-batch empirical accuracy and the inspected page 16 plots do not establish universal exactness; the interleaved isam-convergence extraction is not used as a convergence theorem. The paper explicitly says updates are not constant time and large loop closings can be as expensive as a batch solution. That counterqualification is retained rather than hidden behind typical-case locality. Zero new retrievals. Historical SAM/iSAM2 PDF GETs 2026-09-06T01:11:50.461–01:12:06.713Z and Cadena GET 2026-09-06T01:13:31.236–01:14:02.499Z reported HTTP200; contemporaneous body hashes and redirect histories were not recorded. Retained SAM manuscript and April 2011 iSAM2 draft are not certified publisher versions; Cadena v4 is dated January 30, 2017 with a 2016 journal citation. Current review covered 28 literal/context bindings and iSAM2 images9/16, not whole papers or current liveness. Native source provenance: validation/brand-v2-editorial/source-recovery-20260906/convergence-state-smoothing-integration-20260913/source-proof.json. All three originals and five endpoints compose atomically. Article date, other originals and held factor-graph glossary preserved. Routine correction authority is not personal source certification or release acceptance.",
            "compound": {
              "planId": "state-smoothing-13-20260913",
