                  "supportingPassage": "In particular we show that form closure of any two-dimensional bounded object with piecewise smooth boundary (except a circle) can be achieved by four fingers. For three dimensions, we prove that form closure of any bounded object with piecewise smooth boundary can be achieved with 12 fingers if and only if the object does not have a rotational symmetry (in which case, of course, form closure is not achievable, since no moment along the axis of symmetry can be opposed). We also show that, under very general conditions, form closure of three-dimensional objects without rotational symmetries can be achieved with seven fingers."
