                  "partId": "gp7-mss-algorithmic",
                  "citationId": "mishra-1987",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01840373",
                  "supportingPassage": "We study three cases in detail: (i) the body is at equilibrium, (ii) the body is under some constant external force/torque, and (iii) the body is under a varying external force/torque. In each case we obtain tight bounds on the number of fingers needed to obtain grip. We also present efficient algorithms to synthesize such positive grips for bounded polyhedral/polygonal objects; the number of fingers employed in the grips synthesized by our algorithms match the above bounds. The algorithms run in time linear in the number of faces/sides."
                }
