                  "citationId": "realsense-tuning-2026",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://dev.realsenseai.com/docs/tuning-depth-cameras-for-best-performance/",
                  "supportingPassage": "Stereo depth computation depends on determining matches between left and right images. If there are repetitive structures in the scene, like fences or wire-grids, this determination can become ambiguous. One of the tools we have for determining confidence is the advanced API setting “DSSecondPeakThreshold.” The RealSense D4 VPU determines match scores for both the best match as well as the second best match – if the best match is of similar quality to the second best match, then it may well occur due to aliasing resulting from repetitive structures – how different the two matches need to be is determined by the “DSSecondPeakThreshold” parameter. By increasing its value, more depth results will appear as black, or zero, reducing the number of matches resulting from aliasing."
                },
                {
