                  "supportingPassage": "### 6.2 Semi-supervised video object segmentation\n\n|     |     |     |     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Method | 1-click | 3-click | 5-click | bounding box | ground-truth mask‡ |\n| SAM+XMem++ | 56.9 | 68.4 | 70.6 | 67.6 | 72.7 |\n| SAM+Cutie | 56.7 | 70.1 | 72.2 | 69.4 | 74.1 |\n| SAM 2 | 64.7 | 75.3 | 77.6 | 74.4 | 79.3 |\n\nTable 4: Zero-shot accuracy across 17 video datasets using different prompts. We report average accuracy for each type of prompt (1, 3 or 5 clicks, bounding boxes, or ground-truth masks) in the first video frame (‡: this case directly uses masks as inputs into XMem++ or Cutie without SAM).\n\nWe evaluate the semi-supervised video object segmentation (VOS) setting ( [Pont-Tuset et al., 2017](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#bib.bib77 \"\")) with click, box, or mask prompts only on the first frame of the video. When using click prompts, we interactively sample either 1, 3 or 5 clicks on the first video frame.\n\nSimilar to the interactive setting in § [6.1](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#S6.SS1 \"6.1 Promptable video segmentation ‣ 6 Zero-shot experiments ‣ SAM 2: Segment Anything in Images and Videos\"), we compare to XMem++ and Cutie, using SAM for click and box prompts, and in their default setting when using mask prompts. We report the standard 𝒥&ℱ\\\\mathcal{J}\\\\&\\\\mathcal{F} accuracy ( [Pont-Tuset et al., 2017](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#bib.bib77 \"\")), except for on VOST ( [Tokmakov et al., 2022](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#bib.bib90 \"\")), where we report the 𝒥\\\\mathcal{J} metric following its protocol. The results are in Table [4](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#S6.T4 \"Table 4 ‣ 6.2 Semi-supervised video object segmentation ‣ 6 Zero-shot experiments ‣ SAM 2: Segment Anything in Images and Videos\"). SAM 2 outperforms both methods on the 17 datasets. The results underline that SAM 2 also excels at the conventional, non-interactive VOS task with mask input, for which these other works are specifically designed. Details are in § [F.1.3](https://arxiv.org/html/2408.00714#A6.SS1.SSS3 \"F.1.3 Semi-supervised VOS evaluation details ‣ F.1 Zero-shot video tasks ‣ Appendix F Details on zero-shot transfer experiments ‣ SAM 2: Segment Anything in Images and Videos\")."
