            "note": "RETAINED-CROSS-scene-representation-2-20260907: original claim \"Point cloud is one 3D sample per returned ray, unordered, with no connectivity; a network reading one must be invariant to the ordering of its own input\"; previous verdict \"V\". Cut the universal one-sample-per-returned-ray and no-connectivity definition; the paper defines a point set and its permutation property without requiring that sensor origin. September 7 source-backed implementation under Josef's actual \"fix it all!\" instruction; no personal source certification. Verified retained passages PN-order, PN-perpoint; original events b6778e9d:64:2. Review is not a new fetch or whole-article/P1 acceptance.",
            "compound": {
