            "claim": "Four named components use supplied multi-view images and robot MDH parameters. Mesh assets and measured scene layout alignment connect reconstruction to Isaac Sim. Real-world scene measurement and layout matching are required, not inferred physics from images alone. The evaluator feeds rendered images to a policy, executes actions in Isaac Sim physics, then renders the resulting state. The ring-toss evaluation uses ten trials with up to three grasp attempts per trial, not thirty independent trials. Real-data-model placement differs between hardware (90%) and simulation (30%). Novel-scene table/prose results disagree; rendering and replay are not general physical-fidelity or safety guarantees.",
