            "sourceChecked": "lowry-2016-place-recognition (QUT eprint of IEEE T-RO 32(1):1-19, sec. I: \"whether or not the current visual information is from a place already included in the map\", \"multiple places in an environment may look very similar, a problem known as perceptual aliasing\", \"may not always be revisited from the same viewpoint\"; secs. IV-V on illumination and seasonal change)",
            "note": "Original four-cell tuple (JSON): [\"Place recognition decides from sensor data alone whether this is somewhere the robot has been; the same place changes with viewpoint, illumination and season, and different places can look alike\",\"lowry-2016-place-recognition (QUT eprint of IEEE T-RO 32(1):1-19, sec. I: \\\"whether or not the current visual information is from a place already included in the map\\\", \\\"multiple places in an environment may look very similar, a problem known as perceptual aliasing\\\", \\\"may not always be revisited from the same viewpoint\\\"; secs. IV-V on illumination and seasonal change)\",\"V\",\"\"]. Original tuple SHA256: 58d9b23b2bcdbbfbdbc38b6a33827fcdbafde7bdd1719e79d429500bb873b449. Historical source label retained as a lead, not proof. Source-auditor review 2026-09-08T20:20:57.290Z, worker7355c3bc. Lowry retained QUT PDF: original GET call 2026-09-06T01:14:45.801Z, result 2026-09-06T01:15:27.766Z, HTTP200 and2458048 bytes then. The introduction explicitly asks whether a current image depicts a mapped place; the three-module description allows motion or transition information to inform belief. This corrects the universal sensor-data-alone claim without defining every place recognizer or requiring an exact robot pose. The introduction separates appearance change from perceptual aliasing between distinct places and revisits at different viewpoints. Section IV/V describes illumination and seasonal-condition failures; these are not asserted to be identical mechanisms or universal failure rates. The QUT cover bridges this author manuscript to the 2016 IEEE T-RO issue and DOI while warning it may not be the Version of Record. Its ordered seven-person printed byline includes Sünderhauf and the full Leonard/Milford initials. The body says submitted for review on 18 March 2015; that is not the issue year. Current review is not a new fetch, current-liveness check, or original contemporaneous PDF hash/redirect-chain certification. Source proof: validation/brand-v2-editorial/source-recovery-20260906/convergence-place-slam-backends-integration-20260908/source-proof.json; the immutable packet retains literal supporting and counterpassages. Josef's September7 'fix it all!' authorizes routine source-backed correction, not personal source certification, whole P1, article-date advancement or release acceptance. Only originals32/34/35 are in scope;34/35 share an atomic article span. ORB26/27/31/33 and the prior DSO/neural/pointmap/costmap corrections are preserved.",
            "compound": {
