          {
            "claim": "iSAM2 uses a Bayes tree for incremental reordering and relinearisation: it re-eliminates affected cliques and their ancestors, then reattaches unaffected subtrees. Thresholded state updates trade some accuracy for speed, and large loop closures can cost as much as a batch solve.",
            "line": 384,
