            "claim": "Cadena and colleagues describe sparse landmark maps built from discriminative features and dense geometric models better suited to obstacle avoidance and planning; dense models also appear in visual SLAM. They assess representations by storage size, construction cost and usefulness for the task, and describe more efficient volumetric storage schemes such as octrees and voxel hashing.",
