            "sourceChecked": "cadena-2016 sec. III-A/III-B (\"dense representations attempt to provide high-resolution models of the 3D geometry; these models are more suitable for obstacle avoidance\", against landmark-based sparse maps built from \"discriminative features\")",
            "note": "Original four-cell tuple (JSON): [\"A sparse landmark map localises well and cannot be used for collision checking, while a dense volumetric map does the reverse at much greater cost\",\"cadena-2016 sec. III-A/III-B (\\\"dense representations attempt to provide high-resolution models of the 3D geometry; these models are more suitable for obstacle avoidance\\\", against landmark-based sparse maps built from \\\"discriminative features\\\")\",\"V\",\"\"]. Original tuple SHA256: 94bff6b527a9c129b183b01441a9fdbe61d442bd38a0d8e3f41a740b3cdbafcb. Historical source label and locator errors retained as leads, not proof. Source-auditor review 2026-09-08T21:01:25.692Z, worker28989366. Retained original request window 2026-09-06T01:13:31.236Z–2026-09-06T01:14:02.499Z: HTTP200, 6691958 bytes then; redirect chain and contemporaneous fetch hash were not reported. No fresh fetch or current-liveness claim. SectionV describes sparse 3D landmarks corresponding to discriminative features and possibly uncertain associations. It does not prove sparse maps intrinsically cannot support collision-related tasks; the absolute prohibition is removed. SectionV distinguishes high-resolution raw geometry suited to obstacle avoidance from boundary/spatial-partitioning representations suited to planning, manipulation and contact reasoning. The replacement preserves this task utility without claiming all dense maps solve every task. The dense-model paragraph explicitly describes monocular direct SLAM estimating trajectory and geometry. The feature/direct counterpassage discusses texture, compute and joint-estimation caveats, so dense geometry is not the reverse of localisation. Optimal Representations compares domain, conciseness, ease of creation and efficacy for the task and leaves a general choice framework open. The robot/environment/performance discussion likewise demands scope. No dense-versus-sparse benchmark or universal cost ranking is invented. The spatial-partitioning paragraph names more efficient octrees, and the high-level-representation discussion says voxel hashing can partially mitigate raw point-cloud/TSDF memory burden. Semantic mapping addresses further task meaning; the final claim does not equate geometric density with semantic sufficiency. Original supporting/counterpassage bytes and event provenance: validation/brand-v2-editorial/source-recovery-20260906/convergence-occupancy-map-tradeoffs-integration-20260908/source-proof.json. Moravec ICRA venue expansion remains unestablished; no whole-P1 claim. Cadena current2e3 metadata correction is preserved, including2016 journal/2017v4 printing distinction. Josef's September7 'fix it all!' authorizes routine source-backed repair, not personal source certification, article-date advancement or acceptance. Only originals4/5 and36/37 are applied as their respective atomic pairs; local occupancy/planner/confidence/footprint/figure45 and ORB26/27/31/33 remain outside scope.",
            "compound": {
              "planId": "occupancy-map-tradeoff-scene-36-20260908",
