            "supportingPassage": "C. Perception As range and resolution of depth sensing technologies have improved, so too have world representations for modeling a robot’s environment. To leverage these improvements, a layered costmap approach is used, allowing the user to customize the hierarchy of layers from various sensor modalities, resolutions, and rate limits. A layered costmap allows for a single costmap to be coherently updated by a number of data sources and algorithms. Each layer can extend or modify the costmap it inherits, then forward the new information to planners and controllers. While the costmap is two dimensional, STVL maintains Those used for experiments are as follows: Static Layer: Uses the static map, provided by a SLAM pipeline or loaded from disk, and initializes occupancy information. Inflation Layer: Inflates lethal obstacles in costmap with exponential decay by convolving the collision footprint of the robot. Spatio-Temporal Voxel Layer: Maintains temporal 3D sparse volumetric voxel grid that decays over time via sensor models from the laser and RGBD cameras.",
