                  "supportingPassage": "# Project Go-Big: Internet-Scale Humanoid Pretraining and Direct Human-to-Robot Transfer\n\nSeptember 18, 2025\n\nHelix previously focused on upper-body manipulation tasks like [laundry folding](https://www.figure.ai/news/helix-learns-to-fold-laundry), [dishwasher loading](https://www.figure.ai/news/helix-loads-the-dishwasher), and [package reorientation](https://www.figure.ai/news/scaling-helix-logistics). But in addition to manipulation, humanoids need to be able to intelligently _navigate_ to be useful in homes—finding paths through clutter, repositioning for tasks, and moving fluidly around people and objects.\n\nWe’re excited to share that Project Go-Big has already delivered a promising initial learning result for Helix: **direct transfer from human video to robot behavior**. Using **100% egocentric human video data,** collected passively as people do behaviors in real Brookfield homes, we trained Helix to translate human navigation strategies directly into robot control. Remarkably, this approach required **no robot demonstrations** whatsoever.\n\nVideo 3: After training on 100% human video only, Helix has learned to navigate cluttered spaces from natural language input."
