ed to be constant and in the direction of the robot.\" Discussion: \"even though the 1600 mm/s is an accurate assessment of normal walking speeds, it may be more prudent to instead use the worst-case assumption of 2000 mm/s from ISO 13855 to accommodate instantaneous rapid motions and the uncertainties associated with operator detection.\" Source-internal inconsistency stands recorded (S); the article's wording follows §III, the passage the instrument's constant is drawn from.",
