            "note": "Evidence completion via the UCLA Biomechatronics Lab public mirror of the editorial PDF plus one precise article-span correction: the editorial prints the Level 0 motion-scaling sentence, the practicing-medicine/medical-societies passage with the licensing possibility, and the $31M-vs-$94M / 10-vs-54-month 510(k)-vs-PMA figures; it does NOT state risk tolerance is 'the binding constraint' - it states risk tolerance is expected to change as autonomous machines become commonplace. Clause corrected to the printed wording.",
            "compound": {
